description: |
  MegaMmap is a software distributed shared memory (DSM) system that enables
  efficient processing of data-intensive workloads exceeding main memory capacity.
  It intelligently tiers data across DRAM, NVMe, SSD, and HDD storage to provide
  high-speed access to critical data while minimizing memory consumption.

  The system features workload-aware data organization, adaptive eviction policies,
  and intelligent prefetching to reduce DRAM consumption while maintaining competitive
  performance for various HPC applications including KMeans clustering, DBSCAN,
  random forests, and scientific simulations.

